   "content": [
      {
         "id": "SECTION_prerequisites",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><span id=\"htZoomImageMsg\"></span></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_introduction",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>Introduction</h3>Let's start by looking at some musical instruments found in Caral, Peru, as shown in <b>Figure 1</b>:</p><p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"img0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img0', '0%')\" class=\"imgcenter\"  style=\"width: 35%\"/><b>Figure 1</b>: Section of painel found in archaeological site of Caral, courtesy of © ZonaArqueólogicaCaral (<htcite0> ; <htcite1>). Photo taken on <htdate2>, during a visit to the site.</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "720f6dfd-4b86-4e07-a887-1010e1041a4d",
                     "text": "Ruta Caral",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "11",
                        "day": "02"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "03c3743c-d268-4730-ba8e-d36b5c49e781",
                     "text": "Youtube - Caral Perú Oficial",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "11",
                        "day": "02"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2024",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  },
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2024",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  },
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2017",
                     "month": "6",
                     "day": "13"
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "In this image, we have 32 flutes aligned vertically side by side.",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "In this image, we want to count how many flutes there are at the top.\n\nWith that in mind, let's pause for a quick reflection before moving on.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection question_mark\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-brain\"></i></div><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\"><b>Reflection 1: Couting with our body</b><br />There are more musical instruments in <b>Figure 1</b>  than we have fingers on our hands. How can we count these instruments?</div></div></center></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_together",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>Together we are capable</h3>When we cannot count alone, we can ask for help. This way, we can count:</p><p><table class=\"tawapukllay\"><tr><th colspan=\"2\">First person</th><th colspan=\"2\">Second person</th><th colspan=\"2\">Third person</th><th>Fourth person</th></tr>  <tr><td><img id=\"img5900\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img5900', '0%')\" /></td><td><img id=\"img5901\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img5901', '0%')\" /></td><td><img id=\"img5902\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img5902', '0%')\" /></td><td><img id=\"img5903\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img5903', '0%')\" /></td><td><img id=\"img5904\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img5904', '0%')\" /></td><td><img id=\"img5905\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img5905', '0%')\" /></td><td><img id=\"img5906\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img5906', '0%')\" /></td></tr></table></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p>Counting with the help of others solves our problem again. But look at <b>Figure 2</b>, taken in Copán, Honduras. It has the biggest known text from the Maya region:</p><p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"img8\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img8', '0%')\" class=\"imgcenter\" style=\"width: 35%\"/><b>Figure 2</b>: Altar, stele, and the largest hieroglyphic text at the Copan site (<htcite0>). Photo taken on <htdate1>, during a visit to the site.</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "1e007481-9bd3-4a09-ad4d-6e812fe79641",
                     "text": "Instituto Hondureño de Antropologia e Historia",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "02",
                        "day": "02"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2024",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  },
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2017",
                     "month": "6",
                     "day": "13"
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "An altar, a stela, and the largest hieroglyphic inscription at the site, constructed in a ladder-like format.",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p>This hieroglyphic text, in the background of the image, needs many people to count everything. Let's think of another solution:</p><p><center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection question_mark\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-brain\"></i></div><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\"><b>Reflection 2: Thinking together</b><br />Looking at your fingers, can you find another way to count?</div></div></center></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_ancient",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>Another solution</h3>The need to count did not appear recently. It has existed for a long time, since before there were cities or houses. We know this because of scientists who found bones with marks in different places (<htcite0> ; <htcite1> ; <htcite2>):</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a4f22e25-5839-407f-a1aa-634521d52b42",
                     "text": "González Redondo, Francisco A., et al.",
                     "page": "pp. 174 - 177, 180 - 182",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2010",
                        "month": "06",
                        "day": "12"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "ceffba8a-43be-4de3-a5c8-27cdf81311b1",
                     "text": "Puente, Francisco Barriga",
                     "page": "pp. 21 - 23",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2020",
                        "month": "07",
                        "day": "25"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "cd61bc64-1358-4bfd-b343-3629facaa3b4",
                     "text": "González Redondo, Francisco A.",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "10",
                        "day": "27"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2010",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  },
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2020",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  },
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2024",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"img9\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img9', '0%')\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Figure 3</b>: Representation of baboon bone adorned with markings. This image, credited to Enrique Silván Pobes, is featured in the scholarly work of Francisco A. Gonzáles Redondo et al.<br />The original is available in ResearchNet (<htcite0>), and its inclusion here is made possible by the authorization of Doctor Francisco A. Gonzales Redondo.</p><p>Over the centuries, people used many numbering systems. Some of them are still used today. In the next sections, we show some of today's systems and some that are not used anymore.</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "adaed4fb-9c50-4ef9-ab79-c65f3c0629b8",
                     "text": "González Redondo, Francisco A., et al.",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2010",
                        "month": "02",
                        "day": "01"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2010",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p>Look at the marks on the bones. They look like our fingers.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_conclusion",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>Conclusion</h3>In this text, we learned that with the help of others, we can count even more. But we also saw that this does not solve all problems.</p><p>We also learned that after using our fingers to count, the next step was to make marks. This was not the only solution found. In the next texts, we will look at more options made for counting.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      }
   ],
